---
description: Python quality guardrails (scoped to .py files; zero cost on other turns)
globs: ["**/*.py"]
alwaysApply: false
---

# Python

- Tooling: `uv` for envs/deps, `ruff` (lint + format), `pytest`; type-check new public APIs (`ty`/`pyright`). Skill: `modern-python` (Trail of Bits plugin).
- Type hints on new functions; `from __future__ import annotations` in 3.10+ code.
- No bare `except:`; catch specific exceptions; never swallow errors silently.
- No `shell=True` with interpolated input; prefer `subprocess.run([...], check=False)` + timeouts.
- Parameterized SQL only; never f-string queries.
- Secrets from env/vault, never literals (gitleaks hook blocks commits).
- Tests next to the change; deterministic, no network unless mocked.
- Structure questions → `graphify query` / Serena `find_symbol` before broad reads.
